  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 京\ntitle: capital\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, pictograph, starter]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 亠\nradicalNumber: 8\nonyomi: [キョウ, ケイ, キン]\nkunyomi: [みやこ]\ndistractors: [東, 高, 南]\n---\n\n# 京 — capital\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 亠 (なべぶた, no. 8) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n京 is commonly explained as a picture of a tall building on a mound or hill, which suggests a prominent place and hence a capital city.\nThe old form is debated and 亠 is only the dictionary key, so take the picture as the usual explanation rather than a certain fact.\nIt means \"capital\" (a national capital) and, in numbers, 10^16 (ケイ).\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キョウ | on | [東京](../words/東京.md) とうきょう, 京都 きょうと, 上京 じょうきょう (go up to Tokyo) |\n| ケイ | on | 京浜 けいひん (Tokyo–Yokohama), 京阪 けいはん (Kyoto–Osaka), 京 けい (10^16) |\n| キン | on | rare: 南京 ナンキン (Nanjing) |\n| みやこ | kun | 京 みやこ (capital, literary), 花の京 はなのみやこ |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [東京](../words/東京.md) とうきょう — Tokyo\n- 京都 きょうと — Kyoto\n- 上京 じょうきょう — going to Tokyo (from the provinces)\n\n## Notes\n\n- 京 is read キョウ in both 東京 (\"eastern capital\") and 京都 (\"capital city\"); both names contain 京 but they are different cities. (For a true reversal, compare 田中 and 中田.)\n- 上京 じょうきょう is \"going up to the capital\" (上 as in 上る \"go up\", toward the capital); today it usually means going to Tokyo. The same two characters are also place names where 上 means \"upper\": 上京区 かみぎょうく, the northern \"upper capital\" ward of Kyoto (opposite 下京区 しもぎょうく), and 上京 Shàngjīng, the \"upper capital\" of several medieval northeast Asian states (Balhae, Liao, Jin). The reading differs: じょうきょう for the verb, かみぎょう for the Kyoto ward.\n- **Look-alikes:** 京 vs [高](高.md) (high): 高 has a 口 on top, then a 冂 frame containing another 口, while 京 has a single 口 above 小; compare also 景 (scenery), which adds 日.\n",
